---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import IntakeForm from '../components/IntakeForm.astro';
import { estimatedTimelineField } from '../lib/intake-context';
import HeroBanner from '../components/HeroBanner.astro';
import RequirementsIntakeCta from '../components/RequirementsIntakeCta.astro';
import FinancialClusterNav from '../components/FinancialClusterNav.astro';

const title = 'Portugal HQA Visa Tax - Residence and Filing';
const metaTitle = `${title} | Portugal HQA Residency`;
const metaDescription =
  'Portugal HQA visa tax questions in 2026 turn on whether you become Portuguese tax resident. Confirm filing duties with a licensed tax professional first.';
---

<Layout title={metaTitle} description={metaDescription}>
  <article>
    <header>
      <HeroBanner
        image="/images/portugal-hqa-visa-tax-calculator.jpg"
        alt="Hill of Lisbon houses with terracotta roofs and the dome of Santa Engrácia under a clear sky"
        title={title}
        items={[
          { href: '/', label: 'Home' },
          { href: '/portugal-hqa-visa', label: 'Portugal HQA Visa' },
          { href: '/portugal-hqa-visa-cost', label: 'Cost' },
          { label: 'Tax' },
        ]}
      />
      <div class="bg-background">
        <div class="site-container py-24 md:py-32">
        <p class="max-w-3xl">
          Portugal HQA visa tax questions are about whether living and working here makes you a Portuguese tax resident, and what that does to employment income, foreign assets, and filings in 2026. A residence card is not a tax ruling. This page flags the issues. It does not compute your bill. Instruct a licensed tax professional for numbers. US citizens and green-card holders still have a US overlay; that sits on
          <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-for-americans" class="inline-link">HQA visa for Americans</a>.
          Immigration procedure is a separate file, often with an
          <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-lawyer" class="inline-link">HQA visa lawyer or consultant</a>.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-background-alt">
      <div class="site-container max-w-3xl py-24 md:py-32">
        <section>
          <h2>When Portuguese tax residency can attach</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            Portuguese tax residency is a domestic-law test. In broad terms it looks at days spent in Portugal and at whether the person’s habitual residence or household is here. Crossing a residence-permit threshold does not automatically answer that test, and staying under a day-count you read on a forum does not automatically keep you non-resident. Treat 2026 day-counts and “habitual residence” definitions as items for tax counsel, not for this site.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>

    <RequirementsIntakeCta
      source="/portugal-hqa-visa-tax"
      image="/images/portugal-hqa-visa-tax-cta-divider.jpg"
      alt="Lisbon hillside housing used on the HQA visa tax page"
      heading="Map tax residence against an HQA stay"
      copy="Not sure when Portuguese tax residency can attach? Enter your details and our advisory team can help point you in the right direction."
    />

    <div class="bg-background-alt">
      <div class="site-container max-w-3xl py-24 md:py-32">
        <section>
          <h2>What a tax resident usually has to face</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            Tax residents generally report Portuguese-source income, and may have to report worldwide income, under the Personal Income Tax rules in force, subject to double-tax treaties. Social security on employment often follows the contract and the host. Special personal-tax regimes have been rewritten more than once. Do not assume an old NHR article still applies. Employer withholding does not replace an individual return if one is due.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            This is not legal, tax, or immigration advice. Only a professional who has your facts can say whether a treaty, a social-security certificate, or a current incentive statute changes the picture.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-24">
          <h2>Immigration counsel is not a tax filing</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            An immigration lawyer can assemble the permit. A tax advisor can map residency, payroll, and foreign-asset reporting. Some firms do both under separate engagements. Start with
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-lawyer" class="inline-link">HQA visa lawyer and consultant</a>
            for the permit file, and ask them who handles tax if that is not their licence. Role and host tests remain on
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-requirements" class="inline-link">HQA visa requirements</a>.
            Cash outlay to file is
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-cost" class="inline-link">HQA visa cost</a>.
            Capital tickets are not required; see
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-investment" class="inline-link">HQA visa investment</a>.
            When you lodge, use the
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-application" class="inline-link">HQA visa application</a>
            page. The program overview is the
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa" class="inline-link">Portugal HQA visa</a>
            guide.
          </p>
        </section>

        <FinancialClusterNav current="/portugal-hqa-visa-tax" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="bg-cta-tint">
      <div class="site-container flex flex-col items-start gap-6 py-24 md:py-32">
        <h2 class="max-w-3xl">Separate the permit file from the tax-residency file</h2>
        <p class="max-w-2xl">
          This page is informational. It is not legal, tax, or immigration advice. An advisor can introduce immigration counsel and a tax professional rather than treating one invoice as both.
        </p>
        {/* TODO: no backend yet */}
        <IntakeForm source="/portugal-hqa-visa-tax" contextField={estimatedTimelineField('When do you expect to reside in Portugal?')} />
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
